# Heavy binary data: PDFs (~428 MB) and the raw API dump (~3.5 MB).
# Backed up on Google Drive — see the repo README for the link.
_files/*
# ...except its index, which is NOT just a listing of what is on Drive.
#
# `local`, `bytes` and `content_type` are facts only the downloader knows, and
# nothing offline can reproduce them: a fresh clone that regenerates this file
# gets the mapping but loses the local filename and size of all 284 PDFs, and
# the only way back is to re-download them from a university's server.
#
# So the PDFs stay out and their index comes in. It is 828 KB of text.
!_files/index.json
!_files/README.md
_meta/api_dump.json
_meta/chunk_cache/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated by `--stage merge`. NOT committed, on purpose.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every one of these is rebuilt from `_shards/` in about a second, and every
# one of them is rewritten in full by whoever runs merge. Committing a file
# that four people each regenerate means four people conflicting on it in
# every pull request, in a format nobody can hand-merge.
#
# The shards ARE committed. They are the source of truth: one file per
# portion, one owner each, so two people never write the same path.
#
#     python -m engine.crawler.cuet --stage merge
#
# is what you run after `git pull`. See corpus/cuet/README.md.
documents.jsonl
pages.jsonl
manifest.json
# The corpus README, regenerated by merge. A bare `README.md` pattern matches
# at EVERY depth, so this was also hiding `_files/README.md`, which is the note
# that travels to Drive to say how stale the mirrored index is. Anchored to
# this directory, and the one in `_files/` is kept.
/README.md
!_files/README.md
# Rebuilt in full by whoever runs merge, exactly like documents.jsonl. Leaving
# it committed would hand every teammate a 565 KB conflict the first time they
# regenerate the corpus.
_meta/provenance.jsonl
_meta/found_files.json
_meta/found_files.txt
_meta/found_pages.txt
_meta/run.json
_meta/errors.json
